  "configuration_id": "config_005",
  "reason": "Evidence: The current best config (030, multimodal/multiprofile/scvi_n200/resnet50/avgpool/concat, acc=0.632) outperforms its pca_n2000 counterpart (config_018, acc=0.619) by ~0.013, suggesting scvi_n200 may be a superior RNA encoder. However, this comparison conflates encoder quality with potential RNA-image interaction effects. Uncertainty: We lack a clean RNA-only comparison to determine whether scvi_n200 is genuinely a better representation or whether its small edge is specific to the multimodal context. Question tested: config_005 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool) directly contrasts with config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool, acc=0.591) as a single-variable ablation of RNA encoder. Why best next experiment: This is the cleanest available isolation of the RNA encoder variable with all other factors held constant. The result will (a) confirm or refute scvi_n200 as a generally better encoder, guiding all future multimodal experiments, and (b) quantify the RNA-only ceiling so we can better attribute gains in multimodal settings to image contribution vs. encoder quality. Under a limited budget, resolving this foundational variable before further exploring image encoders or fusion strategies is the highest-information-per-experiment choice."
}

